From 111b76f5ea3f7b6b4d4186d1df7db0a8fcc75bf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:22:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(resource-model): describe inference endpoints in the
 status

The gateway resolves a service by reading status.endpoints, but the
model forbade unknown status fields and defined no such field, the JSON
Schema declared a singular "endpoint" string the model rejected, and
OpenAPI left status untyped. No endpoint could ever be stored, so
streaming routes could never resolve an instance.

Add Endpoint(url, ready, instanceId, protocol) and
InferenceServiceStatus.endpoints. The url must be a plain http(s) base
URL without credentials, query or fragment; protocol is "openai-chat"
(POST /v1/chat/completions) or "tgi-generate" (POST /generate_stream)
and tells the gateway which path to call. An endpoint without "ready"
is ready.

Replace the schema's "endpoint" with "endpoints", describe status and
Endpoint in OpenAPI, and drop the cross-representation test's
workaround for the old field.
